# Plan the approach to a grasp, without executing it.
#
# Splitting planning from execution is the point. Today a failure anywhere in
# pick_one comes back as one boolean, so "no IK solution at that pose", "the
# planner could not find a path" and "the arm was already in collision before
# it started" are indistinguishable, and the placement benchmark records all
# three as failed_stage="motion". A cell that cannot say which of those it hit
# cannot be diagnosed from its logs, and the fix for each is different.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped target   # object top, base_link frame
float64 approach_height 0.12       # metres above the target for the pre-grasp
bool front_constraint true         # keep the elbow out of the camera view
---
bool success
moveit_msgs/RobotTrajectory trajectory
uint8 NONE=0
uint8 NO_IK_SOLUTION=1             # the pose is unreachable
uint8 START_STATE_IN_COLLISION=2   # the arm is already touching something
uint8 NO_PLAN_FOUND=3              # reachable, but no collision-free path
uint8 TARGET_OUT_OF_WORKSPACE=4
uint8 failure
string message
float64 planning_time_s
---
float64 elapsed_s
uint8 attempt
